  "scientific_gaps": [
    "Raw full k-space/sensitivities and phantom visible in data; no blind condition established. Source synthetic Shepp-Logan is not acquired patient brain MRI.",
    "128x128x8 coil-last after removing batch; centered FFT axes(0,1), normalization1/128 and inverse128. Arbitrary intensity, no physical spacing, patient orientation or k-space frequency calibration.",
    "R2 even phase-encode rows plus ACS54..73 gives74/128 sampled lines, effective1.73 acceleration, not exactly50% acquisition. Mask is preprocessing rule, not native raw missing data.",
    "GRAPPA infers mask by first-coil magnitude>0; true acquired zero could be mistaken as hole. Retained acquired coil0 has no exact zeros, so hypothetical hazard is not an observed native failure.",
    "Kernel5x5 with zero-padded ACS boundaries; lambda0=lambda*norm(S^H S)/number_sources, not bare0.01 ridge. Learned ACS weights/filled k-space/RSS not calculated here.",
    "Source main compares full-data RSS and writes ground_truth.npy; generic chooses that before bare phantom data/ground_truth.npz. Reference changes if evaluation file absent.",
    "Source SSIM uses skimage local structural_similarity with reference range; generic SSIM is global mean/variance surrogate using max(reference), not same metric. Nested source metrics are not top-level thresholds.",
    "Filesystem generic scoring uses unscaled range NRMSE; no-filesystem fallback instead flux-normalizes output and uses relative L2 NRMSE against a 2D NPY reference. Neither route was executed here."
  ],
